CORE dfcc-only
before.c
--dfcc main --replace-call-with-contract function
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[function\.precondition\.\d+\] line 3 Check requires clause of contract contract::function for function function: FAILURE$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.1\] line 10 static array parameter .* must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\*\* 2 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A contract on a later declaration keeps the stronger minimum from an earlier
declaration that used a different parameter name, so the generated requires
clause demands four elements rather than the contract declaration's two.
